@c -*-texinfo-*-
@node math-delaunay Manual
@chapter Crate @code{math-delaunay}
@cindex math-delaunay
@cindex Voronoi

@code{math-delaunay} is a faithful Rust port of D3's
@code{d3-delaunay}. It computes Delaunay triangulations and Voronoi
diagrams, using @code{delaunator} as the triangulation backend, and is
consumed by @ref{gpui-d3rs Manual} for spatial visualisations.

@menu
* math-delaunay User Guide::
* math-delaunay Developer Guide::
@end menu

@node math-delaunay User Guide
@section User Guide

This crate has no user-facing surface. It powers Voronoi-style charts
(directivity maps, polar plots) inside the desktop player.

@node math-delaunay Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading Key types

@table @code
@item Delaunay
Delaunay triangulation from a set of 2D points.
@item Voronoi
Voronoi diagram derived from a Delaunay triangulation, clipped to a
bounding box.
@end table

@subheading Example

@example
use math_delaunay::Delaunay;

let points = vec![(0.0, 0.0), (1.0, 0.0), (0.5, 1.0)];
let d = Delaunay::from_points(&points);
let v = d.voronoi([0.0, 0.0, 2.0, 2.0]);
if let Some(cell) = v.cell_polygon(0) @{
    println!("Cell 0 has @{@} vertices", cell.len());
@}
@end example

@subheading Module layout

@table @code
@item delaunay.rs
Triangulation construction and queries.
@item voronoi.rs
Voronoi diagram computation and cell polygon extraction.
@end table

@subheading Testing

@example
cargo test -p math-delaunay
@end example
